-- =========================================================================
-- module social where — the Social capability HIERARCHY (3 classes).
--
-- typed-function-references · FenelModule-retirement Phase FM-retire-3. The 3
-- hand-written `ClassSeed`s exported as `socialTypeclasses` from
-- `engine/src/modules/social.ts` are RETIRED in favour of these `.fenel` class
-- records. Each is authored super-as-FIELD — the SAME shape the std capability
-- hierarchy (`HasHTTP` / `HasSocialMedia` / `HasTelegramBot` in
-- `fenel/std/typeclass-specs.fenel`) already uses: a superclass obligation is a
-- record field whose type is a registered class applied to the class param
-- (`social: Social platform`), NOT `=>` sugar (Fenel has none). `seedFromType`'s
-- field-type classifier (`effect-dispatch.ts:isSuperclassField`) erases that
-- field from the dispatch method set and stamps `seed.supers` in the
-- `{class: Id<Social>, args:[{$var:"platform"}]}` shape the deleted hand-written
-- `supers:[]` arrays carried — so `spec-records.ts:resolve` reads it unchanged.
--
-- Registered in `system-entities.ts` via `seedFromType(…, {isRegisteredClass})`,
-- ORDER-SENSITIVE: `Social` (no super) must be `defineClass`'d BEFORE
-- `Conversational` / `Discoverable` (super = `Social`), or `supersOf` silently
-- drops the constraint (Decision #4 of the 7b′ supers derivation).
--
-- FAITHFUL-SCAFFOLD port (Decision 0 = A): `social` is vision scaffolding, NOT
-- launch scope (`design/vision/social-communication.md`). The method sigs `$ref`
-- entities that nothing registers yet (`Post` / `PostId` / `Engagement` /
-- `PostBody` / `Username` / `Query`) — held as a recorded GAP, exactly as the
-- retired TS `ClassMethod`s already `$ref`'d undefined names. The lone fix:
-- `list_recent`'s `limit` was typed `Int` (no `Int` entity exists — a stale
-- name); it is now `Number` (Decision 5).
-- =========================================================================

module social where

-- Social a — the base platform capability: read / create posts, fetch metrics,
-- list recent posts for a user. (`Post` / `PostId` / `Engagement` / `PostBody` /
-- `Username` are held-gap referents — see header.)
Social platform = Social read_post: PostId -> Post create_post: PostBody -> Post get_metrics: PostId -> Engagement list_recent: Username -> Number -> [Post]

-- Conversational a — threaded interaction. Subclass of Social (the `social:
-- Social platform` super FIELD).
Conversational platform = Conversational social: Social platform post_reply: PostId -> String -> Post get_thread: PostId -> [Post]

-- Discoverable a — search + trending feeds. Subclass of Social (the `social:
-- Social platform` super FIELD).
Discoverable platform = Discoverable social: Social platform search: Query -> [Post] trending: [Post]
